dence of Differential HLA Class I-Mediated Viral Evolution in Functional and Accessory/Regulatory Genes of HIV-1</article-title></related-article><counts><page-count count="1"/></counts><custom-meta-wrap><custom-meta><meta-name>citation</meta-name><meta-value>(2007) Correction: Evidence of differential HLA class I-mediated viral evolution in functional and accessory/regulatory genes of HIV-1. PLoS Pathog 3(8): e121. doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.ppat.0030121">10.1371/journal.ppat.0030121</ext-link></meta-value></custom-meta></custom-meta-wrap></article-meta></front><body><p>doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.ppat.0030094">10.1371/journal.ppat.0030094</ext-link></p><p>Correction for:</p><p>Brumme ZL, Brumme CJ, Heckerman D, Korber BT, Daniels M, et al. (2007) Evidence of differential HLA class I-mediated viral evolution in functional and accessory/regulatory genes of HIV-1. PLoS Pathog 3(7): e94. doi:10.1371/journal.ppat.0030094</p><p>Coauthor Tanmoy Bhattacharya's affiliations were listed incorrectly. The correct affiliations are:</p><p><bold>5</bold> Los Alamos National Laboratory, Los Alamos, New Mexico, United States of America,</p><p><bold>6</bold> Santa Fe Institute, Santa Fe, New Mexico, United States of America</p><p>(The second affiliation was incorrectly listed as <bold>7</bold> Department of Computer Science and Engineering, University of Washington, Seattle, Washington, United States of America.)</p></body></article>